synopsis: Do not send two `Content-Type` headers when the handler sets one
packages: servant-server
issues: #1923
description: {
  `Content-Type` is a singleton header field, but when a handler added one
  (for example with `addHeader @"Content-Type"`), servant-server still added
  its own negotiated `Content-Type`, so the response had two. The handler's
  value now replaces servant's on `Verb`, `Stream`, `ServerSentEvents'`,
  `UVerb` and `MultiVerb` endpoints.
}
